      "prompt": "A student claims: \"Oxidation is always losing oxygen; reduction never loses hydrogen.\"\n\nExplain why this definition fails when analyzing the reaction of Magnesium burning in Nitrogen to form Magnesium Nitride (Mg + N₂ → Mg₃N₂). Identify which element changes oxidation state and define redox solely by electron movement.",
