      "skill": "explain"
    },
    {
      "prompt": "Consider the half-reaction: MnO₄⁻ + 8H⁺ + 5e⁻ → Mn²⁺ + 4H₂O.\n\nConstruct a full cell scenario where this acts as the reduction reaction. You must write:\na) The specific oxidation partner that would provide exactly these 5 electrons (use a standard metal).\nb) The combined equation balancing all atoms and charges without net charge.",
      "answer": "\na) Partner: Zn(s) → Zn²⁺ + 2e⁻\n\nCombined: 3Zn(s) + 2MnO₄⁻(aq) + 16H⁺(aq) → 3Zn²⁺(aq) + 2Mn²⁺(aq) + 8H₂O(l)",
      "rubric": "- Selects a metal capable of releasing electrons.\n- Provides the fully balanced equation with correct coefficients and states.",
      "skill": "produce"
    }
  ],
